1
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:05,170
Outta my way, losers!

2
00:00:05,460 --> 00:00:06,580
That dumbass!

3
00:00:06,580 --> 00:00:08,130
Shit! Somebody stop him!

4
00:00:09,210 --> 00:00:11,080
Stop! Stop!

5
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:13,420
We aren't allowed to use the court right n-

6
00:00:19,750 --> 00:00:20,420
Huh?

7
00:00:27,710 --> 00:00:28,670
Look out!

8
00:00:36,130 --> 00:00:38,130
Are you all right, Yoshino?!

9
00:00:38,130 --> 00:00:40,080
Wait! We shouldn't move her around!

10
00:00:40,830 --> 00:00:43,000
Shit. This is a disaster.

11
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:46,830
Hang in there, Yoshino!

12
00:00:47,040 --> 00:00:48,290
Yoshino?

13
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:53,330
Nurse's Office

14
00:00:51,380 --> 00:00:53,290
Okay. That should do it.

15
00:00:53,880 --> 00:00:56,170
You've only suffered a slight concussion.

16
00:00:56,420 --> 00:00:59,080
If you go home and get
a proper day of rest, then you'll be fine.

17
00:00:59,080 --> 00:01:00,540
That's a relief.

18
00:01:01,210 --> 00:01:04,580
What kind of attitude is that?!
She still got hurt just the same!

19
00:01:04,920 --> 00:01:08,170
The basketball team has been causing
way too many problems lately!

20
00:01:08,330 --> 00:01:10,830
You need to quit ruining things for the rest of us!

21
00:01:10,830 --> 00:01:11,580
Mai...

22
00:01:12,460 --> 00:01:15,080
Let it go. I didn't get hurt that badly.

23
00:01:15,080 --> 00:01:17,580
And it's not even Hanazono's fault to begin with.

24
00:01:19,290 --> 00:01:22,830
As captain of the basketball team, please accept
my apologies for all that's happened lately.

25
00:01:23,130 --> 00:01:24,670
There's no excuse for our actions.

26
00:01:25,040 --> 00:01:26,710
I'm deeply sorry.

27
00:01:48,880 --> 00:01:52,000
Rikukaikuu doko ni ikou

28
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:54,460
Ahiru no Sora

29
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:55,040
Kimi o sasoitai na

30
00:01:55,420 --> 00:01:59,880
Monogatari wa hajima tterunda

31
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:05,580
Okubyou kaze mo recycle

32
00:02:05,580 --> 00:02:08,580
Mayotteru senaka oshite

33
00:02:08,580 --> 00:02:13,790
Give and go! Isogou

34
00:02:16,380 --> 00:02:21,920
Mogutteita honou ga kaodashite

35
00:02:22,540 --> 00:02:29,170
Kakusenai no sa yume ni mita yume

36
00:02:29,500 --> 00:02:32,580
Tobenai tsubasa demo

37
00:02:32,580 --> 00:02:39,420
Bokura wa habataite sora o kanjitai

38
00:02:39,580 --> 00:02:42,750
Naritai jibun ni naritai

39
00:02:42,920 --> 00:02:49,420
Ima dekinai koto mo ashita wa wakannai ze

40
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:52,880
Waru agaki shiyou

41
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:55,920
Happy go ducky!

42
00:03:06,330 --> 00:03:10,710
The Duck and the Kite

43
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:10,710
What the hell is that guy's problem?!

44
00:03:11,750 --> 00:03:14,670
I totally HATE jerks like him with a burning passion!

45
00:03:15,830 --> 00:03:18,130
You're bouncing off the walls more than usual.

46
00:03:18,130 --> 00:03:19,000
Of course!

47
00:03:19,290 --> 00:03:23,130
Momoharu said that if we caused any problems
then the team would be disbanded!

48
00:03:23,460 --> 00:03:27,790
If people start thinking that jerk is on the basketball team,
then we'll have major problems!

49
00:03:27,790 --> 00:03:29,460
Well, you're right about that.

50
00:03:30,130 --> 00:03:33,170
That all aside, what's going on with Chiaki?

51
00:03:33,170 --> 00:03:35,380
He's been crying like a baby since yesterday.

52
00:03:35,380 --> 00:03:36,130
Well...

53
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:38,380
Yay!

54
00:03:36,580 --> 00:03:39,960
Apparently two girls showed up
wanting to be the team managers.

55
00:03:40,080 --> 00:03:40,960
Yo.

56
00:03:44,330 --> 00:03:47,790
But they took one look at Chiaki's face
and nope'd right out of here.

57
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:51,040
Huh?

58
00:03:51,580 --> 00:03:53,790
Did we always have a ball like this lying around?

59
00:03:55,290 --> 00:03:57,380
It looks almost ancient.

60
00:03:57,380 --> 00:04:00,330
Oh. I'm pretty sure it belongs to that Kite guy.

61
00:04:00,750 --> 00:04:02,460
He left it behind yesterday.

62
00:04:03,250 --> 00:04:05,830
Whoa. It's really suffered a lot of wear and tear.

63
00:04:06,710 --> 00:04:08,170
Wait, is this because of...?

64
00:04:19,330 --> 00:04:21,080
I can't see, it's too dark.

65
00:04:23,040 --> 00:04:24,830
That's what you're looking for, right?

66
00:04:25,670 --> 00:04:27,960
It seems like you've used that ball for a long time.

67
00:04:28,710 --> 00:04:30,920
And without being on an actual court much.

68
00:04:31,330 --> 00:04:34,670
I was always told never to use
real leather balls outdoors.

69
00:04:35,290 --> 00:04:38,170
Because it would get all messed up, just like yours.

70
00:04:39,710 --> 00:04:43,170
But since I had no court to play on,
mine ended up in a similar state.

71
00:04:43,790 --> 00:04:47,250
I think... you had the same problem, didn't you?

72
00:04:49,330 --> 00:04:51,130
You want to play basketball, right?

73
00:04:51,130 --> 00:04:54,540
So you should apologize to everyone
and ask to officially join the team!

74
00:04:57,630 --> 00:04:59,460
Mind your own damn business.

75
00:05:02,710 --> 00:05:04,830
I hardly even felt that punch.

76
00:05:06,130 --> 00:05:08,790
Go right ahead and beat me up all you want,

77
00:05:09,750 --> 00:05:13,170
but please make a genuine apology
to Yasuhara and the girls' volleyball team.

78
00:05:13,170 --> 00:05:14,540
Screw that!

79
00:05:15,710 --> 00:05:18,460
I ain't wasting my time
playing basketball with you chumps.

80
00:05:18,920 --> 00:05:22,130
There's nothing I hate more than sappy,
team bonding bullshit.

81
00:05:23,330 --> 00:05:27,670
I only care 'bout two things:
the ball and the basket, that's all.

82
00:05:29,580 --> 00:05:32,290
Don't ever bother me with this crap again, shrimp.

83
00:05:36,880 --> 00:05:40,330
Ow! Damn! It really hurts! Shit!

84
00:05:43,540 --> 00:05:46,500
Oh yeah? You managed to deal
with that mess from yesterday?

85
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:49,330
Yeah. I made a formal apology to them.

86
00:05:50,040 --> 00:05:52,460
You're being too much of a suck up, Momoharu.

87
00:05:52,460 --> 00:05:55,670
All you needed to do was tell them
that punk isn't on our team.

88
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:03,040
Right, Tinytown?

89
00:06:03,040 --> 00:06:06,250
You don't want to have anything to do
with that jackass either, right?

90
00:06:08,540 --> 00:06:09,750
Well, I...

91
00:06:11,330 --> 00:06:15,500
I get the sense that Kite guy
isn't as much of a thug as he seems.

92
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:18,580
Huh? What kind of crap are you spouting now?

93
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,040
No, it's just...

94
00:06:20,380 --> 00:06:22,080
I'm getting real sick of all your crazy talk.

95
00:06:21,040 --> 00:06:22,080
E-excuse me!

96
00:06:22,080 --> 00:06:23,040
I'm getting real sick of all your crazy talk.

97
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:25,750
That guy from yesterday is in the gym again!

98
00:06:44,790 --> 00:06:46,460
What the hell happened here?

99
00:06:46,460 --> 00:06:48,880
Hey, Yabuuchi. What's going on?

100
00:06:49,420 --> 00:06:52,580
No idea. It was already over by the time we got here.

101
00:06:58,250 --> 00:06:59,540
What is your problem?

102
00:06:59,040 --> 00:06:59,540
Wait, Sora!

103
00:06:59,670 --> 00:07:01,210
Just what the hell are you thinking?!

104
00:07:01,880 --> 00:07:06,130
Momoharu, Yasuhara, and everyone else on the team
finally came around to playing basketball with me!

105
00:07:06,830 --> 00:07:09,330
We just managed to form ourselves into a proper team!

106
00:07:10,330 --> 00:07:13,830
Is causing trouble for literally everyone
the only thing you know how to do?!

107
00:07:14,500 --> 00:07:16,210
That shit ain't my problem.

108
00:07:16,710 --> 00:07:18,130
Damn you!

109
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,750
Madoka...?

110
00:07:24,080 --> 00:07:26,080
Stop acting like a spoiled brat!

111
00:07:26,580 --> 00:07:28,960
Everybody else around here plays by the rules!

112
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:31,130
You're a basketball player, too, right?

113
00:07:31,500 --> 00:07:34,330
Then you should know how to follow
the basic rules at the very least!

114
00:07:34,630 --> 00:07:37,830
And if you can't manage that,
then just quit and never come back!

115
00:07:41,710 --> 00:07:43,960
You've got some real guts, girl.

116
00:07:44,290 --> 00:07:45,420
What is this all about?

117
00:07:48,330 --> 00:07:50,750
I just became your advisor and already a fight?

118
00:07:51,290 --> 00:07:52,750
I can't believe the nerve of you boys.

119
00:07:53,630 --> 00:07:56,000
Satsuki, the teacher who keeps the student body in line.

120
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:57,790
THIS is who we got for an advisor?

121
00:07:57,920 --> 00:08:01,670
Well, I got saddled with a duty
I wasn't very intent on fulfilling.

122
00:08:02,130 --> 00:08:04,670
I would actually prefer if the team
was disbanded right away.

123
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,920
I take it this was the basketball team's fault?

124
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:10,540
Mr. Satsuki it isn't what you-

125
00:08:10,540 --> 00:08:12,380
I have no interest in hearing what your excuses are.

126
00:08:13,580 --> 00:08:16,420
The condition you agreed to
was immediate disbandment for any trouble caused.

127
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:19,540
And this is a clear case of fighting on school grounds.

128
00:08:20,630 --> 00:08:22,630
Thus, the basketball team is disbanded.

129
00:08:23,460 --> 00:08:24,710
Disbanded?!

130
00:08:24,710 --> 00:08:26,170
Wait a damn minute!

131
00:08:26,170 --> 00:08:27,630
How the hell does that work?!

132
00:08:27,790 --> 00:08:30,630
That jerk pulled this stunt all on his own!

133
00:08:30,630 --> 00:08:33,130
He isn't even a member of the basketball team, anyway!

134
00:08:33,630 --> 00:08:34,580
Oh?

135
00:08:34,580 --> 00:08:37,210
You're telling me that he has
no connection to the team at all?

136
00:08:38,250 --> 00:08:41,040
Is that how you're handling this, Captain?

137
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:43,580
That's not really...

138
00:08:43,710 --> 00:08:45,500
What's the problem, Momoharu?!

139
00:08:45,500 --> 00:08:47,630
Why don't you just make it clear?!

140
00:08:47,630 --> 00:08:49,420
You know this guy isn't one of us!

141
00:08:53,250 --> 00:08:57,250
Payphone

142
00:08:53,790 --> 00:08:56,000
Seriously? She's calling again?

143
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,250
Give me a break.

144
00:08:57,830 --> 00:08:59,710
Hey, what's up? It's me.

145
00:08:59,710 --> 00:09:00,960
Whaddya want now?

146
00:09:08,540 --> 00:09:10,250
Don't fuck with me, shrimp.

147
00:09:10,420 --> 00:09:11,460
Pick it up.

148
00:09:12,250 --> 00:09:14,670
This isn't the time to be off in your own world!

149
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:17,880
Our entire team is in serious trouble because of you!

150
00:09:19,290 --> 00:09:21,170
I fucking told you to pick it up!

151
00:09:21,170 --> 00:09:22,210
Enough!

152
00:09:24,460 --> 00:09:26,500
Kenji Natsume.

153
00:09:26,500 --> 00:09:29,750
Your suspension from school was barely lifted yesterday.

154
00:09:31,750 --> 00:09:33,670
And you'll get even worse for this mess.

155
00:09:34,500 --> 00:09:36,330
Be ready to get expelled.

156
00:09:36,330 --> 00:09:38,580
As agreed, the basketball team will be disband-

157
00:09:38,580 --> 00:09:39,670
Hold up.

158
00:09:43,210 --> 00:09:45,210
I ain't on the basketball team.

159
00:09:46,330 --> 00:09:46,880
Huh?

160
00:09:47,630 --> 00:09:49,540
Don't group me with these losers.

161
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:50,380
They're below me.

162
00:09:51,040 --> 00:09:52,330
Say that again, bitch!

163
00:09:52,960 --> 00:09:53,960
I see.

164
00:09:53,960 --> 00:09:56,130
So you're to blame for everything, then?

165
00:09:58,500 --> 00:09:59,580
Damn right.

166
00:10:03,170 --> 00:10:06,290
It seems you've avoided the worst-case scenario.

167
00:10:07,710 --> 00:10:09,630
How fortunate for you, Hanazono.

168
00:10:14,210 --> 00:10:17,170
BOYS'
BASKETBALL
TEAM

169
00:10:14,710 --> 00:10:17,170
Seriously? We didn't get disbanded?

170
00:10:17,460 --> 00:10:20,290
Shucks, I was already thinking about
which club to join next.

171
00:10:20,290 --> 00:10:21,920
What's your problem with our team?

172
00:10:22,210 --> 00:10:23,420
I mean, come on.

173
00:10:23,420 --> 00:10:26,500
There aren't even any cute girls
who want to be our manager.

174
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:29,000
Oh, jeez. Of all the problems we have, that ain't one.

175
00:10:29,170 --> 00:10:32,640
Well, in any case, we can at least start using the court now.

176
00:10:32,640 --> 00:10:34,520
All's well that ends well, right Momoharu?

177
00:10:37,630 --> 00:10:38,830
Whatever.

178
00:10:42,040 --> 00:10:44,830
Somebody woke up on the wrong side
of the bed this morning.

179
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:49,960
Cut him some slack. I think Momoharu was starting
to take a real interest in that Kite punk.

180
00:10:52,500 --> 00:10:55,880
The good news is, we can get back
to playing basketball again now!

181
00:10:58,130 --> 00:10:59,460
Hey, Chuckie.

182
00:11:00,040 --> 00:11:02,960
Do you know who those guys were that Kite beat up?

183
00:11:02,960 --> 00:11:05,500
One of them was a senior named Nishiwaki.

184
00:11:05,500 --> 00:11:08,710
And I'm pretty sure the rest
were all part of the group he runs with.

185
00:11:10,210 --> 00:11:11,960
What are you asking for?

186
00:11:12,130 --> 00:11:14,130
No reason. Just curious.

187
00:11:19,250 --> 00:11:21,880
Do you think that guy is really going to get expelled?

188
00:11:21,960 --> 00:11:23,920
The whole thing just didn't sit right with me.

189
00:11:24,040 --> 00:11:27,130
I don't think there's anything for you
to feel guilty about, Madoka.

190
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:28,630
Well sure, except...

191
00:11:28,880 --> 00:11:30,790
...I slapped him across the face.

192
00:11:31,290 --> 00:11:34,460
If you hadn't stepped in,
then I would have done it myself!

193
00:11:36,630 --> 00:11:38,040
I had an ace up my sleeve.

194
00:11:38,040 --> 00:11:40,540
A secret attack, the "Execution Punch!"

195
00:11:42,290 --> 00:11:43,290
Was that it...?

196
00:11:43,710 --> 00:11:47,080
Anyway, that guy is just a big coward!
It's why he lashes out!

197
00:11:47,250 --> 00:11:49,540
He deserved a good smack or two!

198
00:11:49,540 --> 00:11:50,540
But still...

199
00:11:51,250 --> 00:11:54,330
...he took responsibility
and admitted to everything he did.

200
00:11:55,580 --> 00:11:59,170
He may be a lot of things, but a coward isn't one of them.

201
00:11:59,960 --> 00:12:00,670
Huh?

202
00:12:00,670 --> 00:12:02,880
Madoka! Homeroom is about to start!

203
00:12:02,880 --> 00:12:04,000
Yeah, okay.

204
00:12:05,830 --> 00:12:06,830
See ya.

205
00:12:11,500 --> 00:12:12,880
Madoka...?

206
00:12:15,830 --> 00:12:18,960
Madoka seemed kind of cold towards me today.

207
00:12:19,330 --> 00:12:22,000
I can't remember, did I do something to upset her?

208
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:24,930
I know for sure that I haven't done anything extreme

209
00:12:24,930 --> 00:12:27,490
like when I ran around the gym buck naked...

210
00:12:29,420 --> 00:12:30,880
I know that ringtone...

211
00:12:34,040 --> 00:12:35,290
It's him!

212
00:12:38,130 --> 00:12:39,250
Hey, is that you Juri?

213
00:12:41,250 --> 00:12:43,500
How many times do I hafta tell you?

214
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:45,750
Don't waste your money on the payphone
and buy some candy instead.

215
00:12:45,920 --> 00:12:47,000
Nuh-uh!

216
00:12:47,420 --> 00:12:50,130
I want to hear your voice way more
than I want any candy!

217
00:12:51,250 --> 00:12:54,290
Dummy. You know that's just wasting your allowance.

218
00:12:55,130 --> 00:12:58,580
It's okay. 'Cuz I get lots and lots of it!

219
00:13:00,960 --> 00:13:02,710
Is mom doin' okay?

220
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:03,670
Yeah.

221
00:13:04,080 --> 00:13:06,130
She's pretty worried about you, Big Bro.

222
00:13:07,130 --> 00:13:08,380
And dad is, too.

223
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:13,330
I don't want to hear anything about him...

224
00:13:15,420 --> 00:13:18,040
Big Bro, be careful not to break your phone this time.

225
00:13:18,460 --> 00:13:20,080
Oops, thanks.

226
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:21,460
Say, Big Bro?

227
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:22,540
What is it?

228
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:25,290
When can I see you again?

229
00:13:27,330 --> 00:13:30,250
Well, this year's inter-high tournament
is gonna be held over there.

230
00:13:30,250 --> 00:13:31,630
In Hiroshima.

231
00:13:32,210 --> 00:13:34,830
I'll see you this summer. Just wait.

232
00:13:35,250 --> 00:13:37,130
Okay! I'm waiting!

233
00:13:41,460 --> 00:13:42,670
Sorry to keep you waiting, Juri!

234
00:13:43,500 --> 00:13:45,630
Dad's coming this way, so I'm hanging up!

235
00:13:46,710 --> 00:13:48,250
Who were you calling?

236
00:13:48,250 --> 00:13:49,290
Don't tell me it was...

237
00:13:49,290 --> 00:13:51,750
Th-the National Weather Service to get the forecast!

238
00:13:52,290 --> 00:13:53,630
I need you to understand.

239
00:13:54,080 --> 00:13:56,630
Kenji isn't a part of our family anymore.

240
00:13:57,170 --> 00:13:59,540
Don't call him ever again, okay?

241
00:14:01,130 --> 00:14:02,130
Okay...

242
00:14:07,040 --> 00:14:08,500
Another goddamn fight?!

243
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:13,460
Kenji! Just how long are you going to keep
dragging my good name through the mud?!

244
00:14:13,880 --> 00:14:18,290
What does it matter? You ain't my real father, anyway.

245
00:14:18,670 --> 00:14:19,750
Just piss off.

246
00:14:21,080 --> 00:14:22,710
Hey! Get back here!

247
00:14:26,380 --> 00:14:27,540
Big Bro!

248
00:14:29,880 --> 00:14:31,420
Can you believe it, Juri?

249
00:14:31,630 --> 00:14:33,400
I'm not the brightest,

250
00:14:33,400 --> 00:14:37,140
but there's a high school basketball coach who actually sent an invite just for me.

251
00:14:37,330 --> 00:14:39,210
What's a "coach"?

252
00:14:39,750 --> 00:14:41,210
An important person.

253
00:14:41,670 --> 00:14:44,810
There's a really strong school in central Hiroshima and their coach is

254
00:14:44,810 --> 00:14:46,800
saying he wants me to play for them.

255
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:48,290
Wow!

256
00:14:48,750 --> 00:14:50,250
Just you watch.

257
00:14:50,250 --> 00:14:51,560
Once I get into high school,

258
00:14:51,560 --> 00:14:55,540
I'll make sure the whole
country learns my name at the inter-high tourney!

259
00:14:55,710 --> 00:14:58,250
Inter-high! I'm so excited!

260
00:15:01,630 --> 00:15:02,580
Kenji.

261
00:15:03,210 --> 00:15:05,210
You're a young adult going into high school now.

262
00:15:06,670 --> 00:15:09,080
It's been decided that you're going
to be moving this spring,

263
00:15:09,670 --> 00:15:11,960
to live with one of your aunts in Kanagawa.

264
00:15:18,290 --> 00:15:20,250
The inter-high, huh?

265
00:15:22,330 --> 00:15:24,080
It's still so far away...

266
00:15:26,250 --> 00:15:27,750
No, it's really not.

267
00:15:28,920 --> 00:15:32,630
If someone important is waiting for you,
then why aren't you taking it seriously?

268
00:15:35,170 --> 00:15:36,670
Are you stupid or what?

269
00:15:37,330 --> 00:15:39,170
There's no way a team like yours can go to th-

270
00:15:39,170 --> 00:15:40,170
We can!

271
00:15:40,460 --> 00:15:43,290
At the very least, I truly believe that we can.

272
00:15:43,710 --> 00:15:45,880
No, we WILL! Without a doubt!

273
00:15:46,080 --> 00:15:47,830
It's impossible and you know it!

274
00:15:50,080 --> 00:15:52,500
Playing basketball with losers like them is waste of time.

275
00:15:54,250 --> 00:15:56,580
I'd make more progress just doing it on my own!

276
00:15:57,040 --> 00:15:58,420
Then tell me...

277
00:15:58,420 --> 00:16:00,540
Why did you tell that person on the phone
to wait for you?

278
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:03,290
You shouldn't be making promises
that you can't even keep!

279
00:16:03,880 --> 00:16:06,040
It's not something you would understand.

280
00:16:06,040 --> 00:16:06,960
But I do.

281
00:16:07,710 --> 00:16:09,170
Yeah! I'll be waiting!

282
00:16:09,960 --> 00:16:11,380
We're in the same situation.

283
00:16:12,130 --> 00:16:16,710
I'm going to reach the inter-high tournament,
along with everyone on the Kuzu High team!

284
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:22,380
Just how deep in the boonies
have you been playing basketball?

285
00:16:23,630 --> 00:16:26,130
Whatever. I'm getting expelled anyway.

286
00:16:27,420 --> 00:16:31,420
I'll give you a test. Then you'll realize
just how goddamn helpless you actually are.

287
00:16:33,080 --> 00:16:34,460
One-on-one.

288
00:16:34,460 --> 00:16:37,210
Come learn what it's really like
to play at the national level.

289
00:16:37,830 --> 00:16:39,130
One-on-one.

290
00:16:40,460 --> 00:16:42,170
The rules are simple.

291
00:16:43,040 --> 00:16:45,540
If you manage to take the ball from me, you win.

292
00:16:45,540 --> 00:16:47,710
I won't take a step outside of this circle.

293
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,000
You're free to move however you want.

294
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:52,210
All right.

295
00:16:52,380 --> 00:16:54,460
Then in the event that I win,

296
00:16:54,460 --> 00:16:58,630
you join our team and swear
to uphold that promise you made on the phone!

297
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:00,920
How dumb can you get?

298
00:17:01,790 --> 00:17:03,290
I'm gonna be expelled either wa-

299
00:17:03,290 --> 00:17:05,170
No excuses, just swear to me!

300
00:17:06,170 --> 00:17:07,500
Fine, whatever.

301
00:17:13,040 --> 00:17:14,960
All I have to do is get the ball.

302
00:17:15,540 --> 00:17:17,540
The rules he set actually work in my favor.

303
00:17:17,920 --> 00:17:19,170
I'll match his pace.

304
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:22,330
And then in the instant that the ball leaves his hand...

305
00:17:23,040 --> 00:17:23,880
...I'll strike!

306
00:17:29,960 --> 00:17:31,290
I didn't even see him move!

307
00:17:31,790 --> 00:17:34,420
You stand no chance. You're too slow.

308
00:17:34,880 --> 00:17:35,830
Ready to quit?

309
00:17:36,380 --> 00:17:38,330
I will NEVER be a quitter!

310
00:17:51,630 --> 00:17:53,830
All talk and no game. We done yet?

311
00:17:54,130 --> 00:17:56,500
I haven't been able to lay even a finger on the ball...

312
00:17:57,380 --> 00:18:01,580
This tiny circle is starting to feel like
we're playing on a full court!

313
00:18:02,250 --> 00:18:05,580
His playstyle is completely different from how he looks!

314
00:18:06,040 --> 00:18:07,630
It's so smooth and fancy,

315
00:18:07,960 --> 00:18:09,380
and requires more than just speed!

316
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:14,210
I can understand now why Momoharu was so invested
in watching this guy play on the court!

317
00:18:14,790 --> 00:18:16,290
The way that he plays basketball...

318
00:18:16,500 --> 00:18:18,170
...is just so captivating!

319
00:18:21,670 --> 00:18:22,670
Is that it?

320
00:18:23,420 --> 00:18:25,790
Your skills hardly amount to anything, as you can see.

321
00:18:26,420 --> 00:18:28,250
He's on a completely different level than me.

322
00:18:28,630 --> 00:18:30,420
There's no way I'm going to get that ball...

323
00:18:30,420 --> 00:18:31,380
Don't give up!

324
00:18:32,500 --> 00:18:33,960
You've almost got it!

325
00:18:33,960 --> 00:18:36,330
Hey, short dude! I believe in you!

326
00:18:38,630 --> 00:18:39,920
Just leave it to me!

327
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:42,420
I'll get that ball no matter what!

328
00:18:55,080 --> 00:18:56,960
Just give it up already.

329
00:18:56,960 --> 00:18:58,080
This will never end.

330
00:18:58,080 --> 00:18:59,460
Not yet.

331
00:19:00,080 --> 00:19:01,670
Just a little more...

332
00:19:01,880 --> 00:19:03,920
...and then that ball is mine!

333
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:09,540
I almost got it!

334
00:19:09,540 --> 00:19:10,250
Whoops!

335
00:19:10,710 --> 00:19:13,830
Just a little more and that ball is mine, dad!

336
00:19:11,500 --> 00:19:12,500
That was a close one.

337
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:18,670
It's right here!

338
00:19:19,080 --> 00:19:20,580
Just a little more...!

339
00:19:20,580 --> 00:19:21,830
Come on! Come on!

340
00:19:21,830 --> 00:19:23,630
Too bad, ya dummy!

341
00:19:24,880 --> 00:19:26,670
Passes are unfair!

342
00:19:28,500 --> 00:19:30,460
So hey, dad?

343
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:31,920
What?

344
00:19:32,630 --> 00:19:34,080
About my birthday...

345
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:36,960
Next week, yeah? Ask for whatever ya want!

346
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:40,130
Okay, then... I want a legit basketball!

347
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:43,040
One of those fancy ones made from real leather!

348
00:19:43,380 --> 00:19:46,080
Our family doesn't have that kind of money! Ya dummy!

349
00:19:46,080 --> 00:19:49,000
I know that! I just wanted to see what you'd say!

350
00:19:56,500 --> 00:20:01,540
I swear, nobody on Earth ever has as much fun
as you playing basketball.

351
00:19:58,880 --> 00:20:01,920
Yamanaka

352
00:20:09,040 --> 00:20:10,170
I did it!

353
00:20:10,750 --> 00:20:12,670
It's mine!

354
00:20:13,330 --> 00:20:14,880
W-wait a sec!

355
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:16,250
That one didn't count!

356
00:20:16,250 --> 00:20:18,040
I won! I won!

357
00:20:18,420 --> 00:20:19,500
Right, everybody?

358
00:20:21,250 --> 00:20:23,250
Did you see? Wasn't I amazing?

359
00:20:24,170 --> 00:20:27,460
I'm the winner! I won and that means...

360
00:20:29,380 --> 00:20:30,040
...I forgot.

361
00:20:31,290 --> 00:20:33,500
What were we betting on again?

362
00:20:33,750 --> 00:20:37,170
He's so stupid. His head must be totally empty.

363
00:20:37,670 --> 00:20:38,540
Is that you, Natsume?

364
00:20:39,790 --> 00:20:41,130
Mr. Satsuki...

365
00:20:41,130 --> 00:20:44,170
We just finished having a school staff meeting
a few minutes ago.

366
00:20:45,670 --> 00:20:47,040
Your punishment has been decided.

367
00:20:47,420 --> 00:20:49,790
You actually are going to be expelled.

368
00:20:53,330 --> 00:20:55,000
As if there was anything else.

369
00:20:56,040 --> 00:20:57,250
Peace out, shrimp.

370
00:20:57,500 --> 00:20:58,750
Keep practicing.

371
00:21:00,830 --> 00:21:03,290
Please wait a moment, Mr. Satsuki.

372
00:21:03,290 --> 00:21:04,130
What is it?

373
00:21:04,130 --> 00:21:09,420
In regards to yesterday's fight at the gym,
there was one important thing that I lied to you about.

374
00:21:10,710 --> 00:21:14,330
The one who beat up all those guys... it was actually me!

375
00:21:16,630 --> 00:21:19,920
Nobody's buying that, you dumbass!

376
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:24,790
Why do you do this, Yasuhara?

377
00:21:24,790 --> 00:21:27,960
Because your lies always make everything
so damn complicated!

378
00:21:29,170 --> 00:21:31,790
What exactly are you boys trying to get at here?

379
00:21:31,790 --> 00:21:32,880
Not much.

380
00:21:32,880 --> 00:21:34,920
I won't deny that a fight happened.

381
00:21:35,250 --> 00:21:36,580
But you know,

382
00:21:36,580 --> 00:21:39,130
you should at least find out what caused it.

383
00:21:45,420 --> 00:21:49,130
We brought along the guys
that got beat up by him yesterday.

384
00:21:49,130 --> 00:21:53,250
They'll tell you what happened,
and I think it'll make you reconsider his punishment.

385
00:21:55,130 --> 00:21:56,210
You guys...

386
00:22:15,290 --> 00:22:18,630
Doredake sora o miagetatte

387
00:22:18,630 --> 00:22:21,920
Boku wa tobenai to kimi wa itta

388
00:22:21,920 --> 00:22:25,130
Ato nankai te o nobaseba

389
00:22:25,290 --> 00:22:28,500
Todoku no darou to naita yoru

390
00:22:28,630 --> 00:22:32,000
Nigedasu koto ni nareteitte

391
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:35,290
Sore ga yowasa dato shitta ano hi

392
00:22:35,290 --> 00:22:39,500
Hajimeyou mata, kyou kara

393
00:22:42,130 --> 00:22:48,130
Taisetsu na mono wa itsudemo soba ni atta

394
00:22:48,130 --> 00:22:54,460
Bokura wa itsumo hitori janai donna toki mo

395
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:57,790
Toberu sa doko made mo kimi wa

396
00:22:57,790 --> 00:23:01,540
Dare yori tataku tataku habataite

397
00:23:01,750 --> 00:23:05,790
Nagashita namida no kazu dake

398
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,750
Tsuyoku narunda

399
00:23:07,750 --> 00:23:11,130
Tsubasa hiroge sekai o megutte

400
00:23:11,130 --> 00:23:14,710
Dare mo shiranai mirai o sagasou

401
00:23:14,710 --> 00:23:19,290
Zutto, zutto, zutto

402
00:23:19,460 --> 00:23:22,960
Aruite yukou saa, issho ni

403
00:23:30,920 --> 00:23:35,420
Ahiru no Sora
Next Time: Kite, His Ball
and the Team's Pain

404
00:23:31,630 --> 00:23:35,250
Next time: "Kite, His Ball, and the Team's Pain."

